pySMESH: StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder owns and frees what it makes, and refuses AddLayers
before GetShrinkGeometry (SMESH V9_16_0).

Defect: the two-step viscous-layer API (SMESH d3c3260cd, 2023-07-25, bos #35147) leaks and
can read an unset pointer.

Symptom:
* ~StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder is empty (StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder.cxx:110-112):
  the StdMeshers_ViscousLayers2D made in the constructor and the
  StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL::ViscousBuilder made by GetShrinkGeometry, with the TmpMesh it
  owns (StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx:828, freed only by ~ViscousBuilder at :884), leak.
* AddLayers called before GetShrinkGeometry dereferences _vlBuilder, which nothing set:
  undefined behaviour.
* A second GetShrinkGeometry replaces _vlBuilder without freeing the first.
* The constructor gives the inner StdMeshers_ViscousLayers2D the builder's own id. Every
  SMESH_Hypothesis enters itself in the generator's map by id (SMESH_Hypothesis.cxx:51-55),
  so the inner one overwrites the builder's entry, and ~SMESH_Gen, which nullifies the
  generator pointer of each hypothesis in its map, misses the builder: a builder that
  outlives its generator then writes to the freed map in its destructor.

Change, in StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder.hxx/.cxx only:
* _vlBuilder starts as nullptr.
* The inner hypothesis takes gen->GetANewId().
* The destructor deletes _vlBuilder and _hyp.
* GetShrinkGeometry deletes the previous _vlBuilder before it makes a new one.
* AddLayers throws SALOME_Exception when GetShrinkGeometry was not called.

Not changed: how the shrink geometry and the layers are computed.
diff --git a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder.hxx b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder.hxx
--- a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder.hxx
+++ b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder.hxx
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@
     
     
     StdMeshers_ViscousLayers2D*                     _hyp;
-    StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL::ViscousBuilder*  _vlBuilder;
+    StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL::ViscousBuilder*  _vlBuilder = nullptr; // pySMESH: set by GetShrinkGeometry
 
     BRepOffset_MakeOffset                     _makeOffset;
     BRepOffset_Offset                     _makeFaceOffset;
diff --git a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder.cxx b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder.cxx
--- a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder.cxx
+++ b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder.cxx
@@ -45,7 +45,9 @@
   : SMESH_2D_Algo(hypId, gen)
 {
   _name = "StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder";
-  _hyp    = new StdMeshers_ViscousLayers2D( hypId, gen );  
+  // pySMESH: a fresh id. The builder's own id would overwrite the builder's entry in the
+  // generator's map (SMESH_Hypothesis.cxx:51-55), so ~SMESH_Gen would not nullify it.
+  _hyp    = new StdMeshers_ViscousLayers2D( gen ? gen->GetANewId() : hypId, gen );
 }
 
 bool StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder::CheckHypothesis(SMESH_Mesh&                          aMesh,
@@ -109,10 +111,14 @@
 
 StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder::~StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder()
 {
+  // pySMESH: free what the builder owns (the offset builder holds its TmpMesh).
+  delete _vlBuilder;
+  delete _hyp;
 }
 
 TopoDS_Shape StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder::GetShrinkGeometry( SMESH_Mesh & theMesh, const TopoDS_Shape& theShape )
 {
+  delete _vlBuilder; // pySMESH: a second call frees the builder of the first
   _vlBuilder  = new StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL::ViscousBuilder( _hyp, theMesh, theShape );
 
   std::string error = "";
@@ -125,6 +131,8 @@
 
 bool StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder::AddLayers( SMESH_Mesh & shrinkMesh, SMESH_Mesh & theMesh, const TopoDS_Shape& theShape )
 {
+  if ( !_vlBuilder ) // pySMESH: there is no offset shape to build on yet
+    throw SALOME_Exception( "AddLayers() needs GetShrinkGeometry() to be called first." );
   bool success = _vlBuilder->MakeViscousLayers( shrinkMesh, theMesh, theShape );
   
   if ( !success )
